Kubernetes Namespace

Today I also learned about Namespaces in Kubernetes and how they help organize and separate resources within a Kubernetes cluster.

What I learned
A Namespace provides a logical boundary for Kubernetes resources.
It helps separate environments such as development, staging, and production.
Resources like Pods, Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, and Secrets can be created inside a namespace.
Namespaces also help with RBAC, resource quotas, and access control.
A namespace does not automatically provide complete network isolation.
Example
Kubernetes Cluster
│
├── dev
│   ├── Pods
│   ├── Services
│   └── Deployments
│
├── staging
│   ├── Pods
│   └── Services
│
└── production
    ├── Pods
    ├── Services
    └── Deployments
Useful Commands
kubectl create namespace dev

kubectl get namespaces

kubectl get pods -n dev

kubectl get services -n dev

Key takeaway:

Namespace → logically organizes and separates Kubernetes resources within a cluster.